  "worked_solution": "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=4f(x)+7,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=4f(x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215498/assets/178f32ee899fe88c09207e080727689f151fa17b1fb5591f2d689e90dcf4e46e.png)\n\n- Then, translate it up by $7$ units to get the graph of $y=4f(x)+7.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215498/assets/5c1e620fbb2d3de5bb27519464b931aa9d7bce9043e2f9e1a33d52897849e31d.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
